# Finding Gold in Data Mining

**Authors:** Flaherty, Bill

## Abstract
Data-mining systems provide a variety of opportunities for school district personnel to streamline operations and focus on student achievement. This article describes the value of data mining for school personnel, finance departments, teacher evaluations, and in the classroom. It suggests that much could be learned about district practices if one had data gathered from instruction, finance, human resources, maintenance, transportation, and food  service all in one unified structure.

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ1017337

